## Recommendation: Use `System.IO.Abstractions`

For `File.*` and `Directory.*` calls, the best approach on .NET 10 is the battle-tested **System.IO.Abstractions** NuGet package — no need to write custom wrappers.

### 1. Install the package

```bash
dotnet add package System.IO.Abstractions
```

### 2. Register in DI (`Program.cs`)

```csharp
builder.Services.AddSingleton<IFileSystem, FileSystem>();
```

### 3. Inject `IFileSystem` into your class

```csharp
using System.IO.Abstractions;

public class ReportGenerator(IFileSystem fileSystem)
{
    public string GenerateReport(string reportName)
    {
        var outputDir = Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable("REPORT_OUTPUT_DIR") ?? "/tmp/reports";

        if (!fileSystem.Directory.Exists(outputDir))
        {
            fileSystem.Directory.CreateDirectory(outputDir);
        }

        var reportPath = fileSystem.Path.Combine(outputDir, $"{reportName}.txt");
        fileSystem.File.WriteAllText(reportPath, content);

        return reportPath;
    }
}
```

### 4. Test with `MockFileSystem`

```bash
dotnet add <TestProject> package System.IO.Abstractions.TestingHelpers
```

```csharp
var mockFs = new MockFileSystem();
mockFs.AddDirectory("/tmp/reports");

var generator = new ReportGenerator(mockFs);
var path = generator.GenerateReport("sales");

Assert.True(mockFs.File.Exists(path));
Assert.Contains("sales", mockFs.File.ReadAllText(path));
```

---

### Bonus: Your `ReportGenerator` also uses other statics

Looking at `Services/ReportGenerator.cs`, you also have `DateTime.UtcNow`, `Environment.*`, and `Console.WriteLine`. For those:

| Static | Recommended approach |
|--------|---------------------|
| `DateTime.UtcNow` | Inject `TimeProvider` (built-in on .NET 10): `services.AddSingleton(TimeProvider.System);` |
| `Environment.*` | Custom `IEnvironmentProvider` wrapping only `GetEnvironmentVariable` + `MachineName` |
| `Console.WriteLine` | Custom `IConsole` or just use `ILogger<T>` |

Want me to generate wrappers for any of those as well?
